# Peer-dependency resolution for this repo.
#
# `legacy-peer-deps=true` is here because the committed package-lock.json contains a
# peer range that npm 10 refuses to install: openapi-typescript@7.13.0 (the latest
# published version) declares `peerDependencies: { typescript: "^5.x" }`, while this
# repo is on typescript@6. Without the flag, a CLEAN CHECKOUT cannot install at all:
#
#   $ npm ci
#   npm error Could not resolve dependency:
#   npm error peer typescript@"^5.x" from openapi-typescript@7.13.0
#
# Nobody noticed for months because an existing node_modules makes `npm ci` moot and
# `npm install` was run with the flag implicitly present in a developer's environment.
# The first CI run on a fresh runner is what surfaced it (NIM-355).
#
# Why the flag and not a version change:
#   - There is no openapi-typescript release that accepts typescript@6 — 7.13.0 is the
#     newest one published, and its cap is upstream's, not ours.
#   - Downgrading typescript to ^5.9 to satisfy that cap would move the whole toolchain
#     (tsc, typescript-eslint, every .d.ts) for the sake of one codegen-only devDependency.
#   - openapi-typescript is a build-time tool whose output is committed
#     (src/api/types.gen.ts, src/api/constraints.gen.ts). It demonstrably works under
#     typescript@6: `npm run gen:api` reproduces the committed files byte-for-byte, which
#     the `codegen` job in .github/workflows/ci.yml asserts on every push.
#
# It lives in .npmrc rather than as a `--legacy-peer-deps` flag in the workflow ON PURPOSE.
# The point of this repo's CI is that a clean checkout installs and builds; if CI passed a
# flag developers don't, the two environments would diverge again and the gate would be
# testing something nobody runs. Dependabot reads .npmrc too, so its PRs resolve the same way.
#
# COST, stated plainly: this relaxes peer checking for the WHOLE project, so a future
# genuine peer conflict is accepted silently instead of failing the install. What actually
# proves the tree is coherent is the lint / test / build / codegen jobs, not npm's peer
# metadata. Remove this file when openapi-typescript widens its peer range to typescript@6.
legacy-peer-deps=true
